# UI Page Headers

## Standard page header
Every page has a consistent header:
```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  [← Back]  Breadcrumb / Title         [Actions]     │
│  (optional sub-text / status line)                   │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Title
- `t-h1` class (Inter Tight, 24px, weight 300, -0.01em tracking).
- Plain English, sentence case, no punctuation.
- For dataset/incident/metric detail pages, title is the resource name.

## Breadcrumbs
Shown on detail pages: `Sources / my-warehouse` or `Incidents / INC-1042`.
- Separator: `/` in `fg-2` color.
- Current page is non-clickable.
- Parent segments are links.

## Actions
Right-aligned. Maximum 2 visible primary actions. Overflow into a `...` menu (shadcn DropdownMenu).

Button sizing: `size="sm"` for header actions. Use `variant="outline"` for secondary, `variant="accent"` for primary.

## Back navigation
`← Back` link on detail pages. Uses `router.back()` if navigated from the list, or explicit list URL as fallback.

## Status line (detail pages)
Below the title: compact status indicators — severity badge, lifecycle status, last updated time, owner.
```
● fail  ·  investigating  ·  opened 2h ago  ·  Jamie Lin
```

## AppShell topbar
- Left: sidebar toggle (≡), app logo.
- Centre: Cmd-K search trigger.
- Right: theme toggle, notification bell (incident count badge), user avatar menu.

Not part of page-level headers — managed by `AppShell` and consistent across all pages.
